## What your endpoint should do

Because delivery is at least once, the same event can arrive more than once, for example when your server processed it but its 200 was lost. Every retry carries the same event id, so deduplicate on it. Respond fast and do the slow work afterward.

```http
POST /hooks/payments HTTP/1.1
Webhook-Id: evt_01JA7Q3M
Webhook-Attempt: 3
Webhook-Timestamp: 1760803200
Content-Type: application/json
```

```python
@app.post("/hooks/payments")
def receive():
    event = request.get_json()
    if already_processed(event["id"]):   # retries reuse the same id
        return "", 200
    queue.put(event)                     # slow work happens later
    return "", 200
```

! Return a 2xx only after you have safely stored the event. A 2xx tells us never to send it again.
